oint (PY6c)"] [524 2 "// any int, not only a C ssize_t (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_math's msum takes bin of a 2000-bit int)"] [550 2 "// slot_nb_divmod's vectorcall_maybe: a __divmod__ or __rdivmod__ set to None is called (TypeError), queue 264"] [578 2 "// PyNumber_Power's ternary_op (PY7: the built-in did ints by int64 and an object only by its __pow__, never the"] [579 2 "// exponent's __rpow__ nor a big int)"] [608 1 "// attrName is getattr's, setattr's, hasattr's and delattr's name: a str, or a str subclass's instance as its str"] [609 1 "// value (queue 203: CPython takes any str; test_dict's test_instance_dict_getattr_str_subclass)."] [630 3 "// with a default: _PyObject_LookupAttr's lookup, a module's missing name answered without its message's work"] [631 3 "// (module_getattro's suppress: no __spec__.has_location, a Python property, called; queue 293)"] [668 3 "// a generator's StopIteration carries its return value (PY7: next() raised a bare StopIteration, the slot's"] [669 3 "// Next ending with nil)"] [688 1 "// sortObjects sorts items in place by key (nil: the items) and reverse, stably: the keys computed in"] [689 1 "// order, then PY5b's SortObjects (list.sort's)."] [742 1 "// noFrameGlobals is the globals of a call with no Python frame: the running __main__'s"] [743 1 "// (_PyEval_GetGlobalsFromRunningMain), else a new dict."] [754 1 "// frameLocals is locals() of a frame (PEP 667): a module's or class's namespace (its mapping when that is no dict;"] [755 1 "// frameNamespace), else a new dict of a function's bound fast locals, cells and free variables, then its extra locals (the proxy's"] [756 1 "// snapshot, _PyEval_GetFrameLocals: a write to it does not reach the frame)."] [759 27 "// a call with no Python frame (an interpreter's call, queue 230)"] [791 1 "// builtinDir is dir(): the scope's names, or an object's __dir__() sorted (PY5c's lookup); without a"] [792 1 "// __dir__, a module's namespace, a type's and its bases', an object's type's and its __dict__'s."] [815 3 "// the object's __dir__ (object's, type's, module's, a class's own: PY5c's), its result sorted"] [831 3 "// the scope's names: a mapping not a dict (exec's locals; queue 219) by its keys"] [833 3 "// PyMapping_Keys: an exact dict's keys, any other mapping's keys() (a dict subclass's own too; py-core-1124:"] [834 3 "// test_builtin's test_general_eval)"] [838 4 "// PyMapping_Keys"] [891 2 "// builtin_input_impl: sys.stdin, then sys.stdout, deleted or None a RuntimeError (py-core-1124: test_builtin's"] [892 2 "// test_input)"] [901 2 "// the readline module imported and both streams the process's terminals (builtin_input's tty path over"] [902 2 "// PyOS_Readline, queue 289): the line by its editor, the prompt its own"] [931 2 "// builtin_input_impl: sys.stdout flushed before the read (queue 551: a real TextIOWrapper's flush too)"] [939 3 "// the fallback's _PyFile_Flush: an error cleared (py-core-1124: test_builtin's test_input, a stdout with no flush)"] [974 1 "// intRound is int.__round__ (long_round): ndigits by __index__ (a TypeError for others), an exact int of the value"] [975 1 "// when it is not negative, else the value rounded half-even to 10**-ndigits (_PyLong_DivmodNear) at any size (queue"] [976 1 "// 328: it was int64's, so a big int or a big ndigits went wrong: test_long's test_round)."] [990 2 "// 10**k past twice |v|: the nearest multiple is 0 (10**k has k+1 digits)"] [995 50 "// Euclidean: 0 <= r < p"] [1003 1 "// roundFloat is float.__round__ (Objects/floatobject.c's double_round): to an int, ties to even, without"] [1004 1 "// ndigits; else the correctly rounded value at ndigits decimal places (round-half-even on the exact decimal"] [1005 1 "// value, as dtoa's mode 3), negative ndigits rounding to tens, hundreds ..."] [1017 2 "// PyNumber_AsSsize_t(o_ndigits, NULL): an ndigits past ssize_t clamped (queue 328: test_float's test_large_n)"] [1034 2 "// the exact decimal value of x, rounded half-even at n places afte